Java Code:
```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Optional;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public List<Optional<Integer>> largestSmallestIntegers(List<Integer> lst) {
    List<Integer> negatives = lst.stream()
        .filter(x -> x < 0)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());
    List<Integer> positives = lst.stream()
        .filter(x -> x > 0)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

    Optional<Integer> maxNegative = negatives.isEmpty() ? Optional.empty() : Optional.of(negatives.stream().max(Integer::compare).get());
    Optional<Integer> minPositive = positives.isEmpty() ? Optional.empty() : Optional.of(positives.stream().min(Integer::compare).get());

    return List.of(maxNegative, minPositive);
}
```
This Java code uses Java 8 streams to filter the negative and positive numbers, and then find the maximum of the negative numbers and the minimum of the positive numbers. If there are no negative numbers, `maxNegative` will be `Optional.empty()`, and if there are no positive numbers, `minPositive` will be `Optional.empty()`. The function returns a list of these two optionals.

